<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:vm="using:Paperbunkr.App.ViewModels"
             xmlns:models="using:Paperbunkr.App.Models"
             xmlns:entities="using:Paperbunkr.Data.Entities"
             xmlns:views="using:Paperbunkr.App.Views"
             xmlns:reader="using:Paperbunkr.App.Views.Reader"
             xmlns:books="using:cYo.Projects.ComicRack.Engine.IO.Provider.Books"
             xmlns:dict="using:Paperbunkr.App.Services.Dictionary"
             xmlns:fi="using:FluentIcons.Avalonia"
             xmlns:conv="using:Avalonia.Data.Converters"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d" d:DesignWidth="700" d:DesignHeight="800"
             x:Class="Paperbunkr.App.Views.BookReaderScreen"
             x:DataType="vm:BookReaderScreenViewModel">

    <!-- "Where am I?" heading trail (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-01-books-reader-screen-reader-accessibility-design.md): Ctrl+Shift+W is the BookReader.AnnouncePosition input-service
         action now (Preferences > Keyboard Shortcuts), so there is no UserControl.KeyBindings here. -->

    <!-- chromeIcon/tocRow/resultRow/deleteRow/sheetOption/themeSwatch styles moved to
         Styles/ReaderChrome.axaml (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-books-reader-hud-redesign-
         design.md), merged app-wide via App.axaml so PdfPageReaderScreen.axaml shares them too. -->

    <Grid x:Name="RootGrid" Background="{Binding Settings.Background}" Focusable="True" FocusAdorner="{x:Null}"
          PointerMoved="OnRootPointerMoved" KeyDown="OnRootKeyDown">

        <!-- Reading pane - real markup rendered via NativeWebView (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-02-
             books-reflow-reader-webview-redesign-design.md), replacing the old ParagraphView/
             TextLayout renderer. Tap-to-toggle-chrome, page-turn, selection, and highlight-tap are all
             driven by the JS bridge (BookReaderScreen.axaml.cs's HighlightScript +
             OnReaderWebMessageReceived) rather than Avalonia routed pointer/key events, since a native
             embedded control doesn't reliably bubble those the way a normal control would.

             Margin="0,56,0,56" reserves dedicated, never-overlapped strips at top/bottom for the
             chrome bars below - the "airspace" problem: a native windowed control (which is what
             NativeWebView is in this package version - no public render-mode switch exists yet to
             opt into Avalonia-composited hosting instead, confirmed by inspecting the installed
             12.0.0 assembly directly, not assumed from docs describing a newer version) always
             composites *above* every Avalonia-drawn element regardless of XAML z-order, so the old
             full-bleed layout made the chrome Borders below permanently invisible no matter what
             IsChromeVisible did - not a bug in the visibility logic itself, a structural one. 56px
             (not the originally-guessed 44/40px) exactly clears each bar's real rendered height -
             Border Padding="10,8" (8px top+bottom) around a 36px chromeIcon button = 52px, plus a
             4px buffer - an under-reservation here would let the WebView's own airspace claim a
             sliver of the button's own clickable area, which is exactly the kind of thing that reads
             as "the button doesn't work" without an obvious visual cue why. The TOC/Bookmarks/
             Highlights/Search/font-sheet overlays were built on the assumption that Popup +
             ShouldUseOverlayLayer="False" (meant to force a real separate top-level OS window,
             which - unlike a plain in-tree overlay - can win the airspace fight against a native
             child HWND) would keep them above the WebView, the same way it was assumed to for the
             small highlight color-picker popup below. Real on-screen testing (2026-09-16 user
             report) showed it does NOT hold for these: every one of them rendered with only its
             first sliver (e.g. just a drawer/sheet header) visible, the rest covered by the WebView.
             Root cause, confirmed via Avalonia's own docs, not guessed: Program.cs's
             Win32PlatformOptions.OverlayPopups = true (added 2026-09-10 for an unrelated ComboBox-
             dropdown freeze fix) makes Avalonia embed EVERY popup into the window's own surface
             regardless of that popup's own ShouldUseOverlayLayer value - a platform-wide override,
             not a per-popup opt-out ("OverlayPopups: Embeds popups to the window when set to true").
             So every overlay in this file has actually been in-process/overlay-layer-rendered since
             2026-09-10, contrary to what ShouldUseOverlayLayer="False" implies - which loses to the
             WebView's native child HWND the same as a plain in-tree overlay would, unlike the
             chrome-bar margin above, which sidesteps the whole problem by never overlapping at all.

             First attempt (same day) hid this WebView entirely (IsVisible bound to !IsAnyDrawerOpen)
             whenever a drawer/sheet was open - functionally correct (no more blocked drawers) but
             lost the original, better behavior: right after this reader was first built, opening a
             drawer showed it above the still-visible (if dimmed-by-scrim) page, not a fully blank
             one. Superseded the same day, once the user pointed that out: TOC/Bookmarks/Highlights/
             Search (ReaderListDrawer.axaml) and the font sheet (ReaderSettingsSheet.axaml) are now
             each hosted in a real, separately-owned Window (OverlayWindowController) instead of a
             Popup - a Window is NOT subject to OverlayPopups, so it reliably renders above this
             WebView the way the original Popup-based approach was always assumed to, restoring the
             original look. This WebView no longer needs to hide itself at all.

             The highlight color/note popup below still relies on the broken Popup assumption and
             has not been verified or fixed - it likely has the same bug; not converted to a Window
             here since it's small and anchored next to a selection/highlight the user needs to keep
             seeing behind it, a different design question than the full-screen drawers. -->
        <!-- Books redesign §5.1 (2026-10-27): the page fills the window again. The chrome is no longer bars in reserved strips but floating
             clusters, each in its own small owned window (ClusterHolder below), so nothing needs to sit beside the native page. -->
        <NativeWebView x:Name="ReaderWebView"
                       NavigationCompleted="OnReaderNavigationCompleted" WebMessageReceived="OnReaderWebMessageReceived"
                       AutomationProperties.AutomationId="BookReaderWebView" />

        <!-- Chrome (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-books-reader-hud-redesign-design.md) - shared
             top/bottom bar control, replacing the two hand-rolled Border bars this screen used to
             declare itself. Mode="TapToHide": no internal behavior difference from PDF's chrome today
             (see ReaderChrome.axaml.cs's own doc comment), IsChromeVisible is still this screen's own
             BookReaderScreenViewModel-driven auto-hide state, just rebound. Previous/Next stay
             Click-driven (OnPreviousButtonClick/OnNextButtonClick raise PreviousRequested/
             NextRequested, handled below the same way the old Click handlers were) since page-turn
             needs the WebView-scroll-first, VM-command-fallback logic that lives in this screen's own
             code-behind, not a pure command. -->
        <!-- The three floating clusters (books redesign §5.2). They live here only while hidden: ClusterWindowController moves each into its
             own small owned window, anchored to RootGrid, while IsChromeVisible is true. Coloured from the book theme. -->
        <Panel x:Name="ClusterHolder" IsVisible="False">
            <reader:ReaderCluster x:Name="NavigateCluster" Part="Navigate"
                                  ClusterBackground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static views:ReaderChromeBackgroundConverter.Instance}}"
                                  ClusterForeground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static views:ReaderChromeForegroundConverter.Instance}}"
                                  ClusterBorder="{DynamicResource PbBorderBrush}"
                                  Title="{Binding BookTitle}" Subtitle="{Binding ChapterTitle}"
                                  BackCommand="{Binding CloseCommand}" ContentsCommand="{Binding OpenTocCommand}" />
            <reader:ReaderCluster x:Name="ActionsCluster" Part="Actions"
                                  ClusterBackground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static views:ReaderChromeBackgroundConverter.Instance}}"
                                  ClusterForeground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static views:ReaderChromeForegroundConverter.Instance}}"
                                  ClusterBorder="{DynamicResource PbBorderBrush}"
                                  SearchCommand="{Binding OpenSearchCommand}"
                                  BookmarkCommand="{Binding ToggleBookmarkCommand}" IsBookmarked="{Binding IsCurrentPositionBookmarked}"
                                  NotesCommand="{Binding OpenNotesCommand}" SettingsCommand="{Binding OpenFontSheetCommand}" />
            <reader:ReaderCluster x:Name="PageCluster" Part="Page"
                                  ClusterBackground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static views:ReaderChromeBackgroundConverter.Instance}}"
                                  ClusterForeground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static views:ReaderChromeForegroundConverter.Instance}}"
                                  ClusterBorder="{DynamicResource PbBorderBrush}"
                                  ProgressFraction="{Binding ProgressFraction}" PartTicks="{Binding PartTicks}"
                                  LeftLabel="{Binding ClusterLeftLabel}" RightLabel="{Binding ClusterRightLabel}"
                                  IsPreviousEnabled="{Binding CanGoPrevious}"
                                  PreviousRequested="OnClusterPreviousRequested" NextRequested="OnClusterNextRequested" />
        </Panel>

        <!-- Screen-reader-only live region (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-01-books-reader-screen-
             reader-accessibility-design.md) - always in the visual/automation tree (never
             IsVisible="False", which risks the peer being dropped from the tree entirely), just
             visually inert. Announces page-turns/chapter-changes and the Ctrl+Shift+W heading trail,
             both written to the same BookReaderScreenViewModel property. -->
        <TextBlock Text="{Binding ReadingPositionAnnouncement}" Opacity="0" IsHitTestVisible="False"
                   AutomationProperties.LiveSetting="Polite" AutomationProperties.Name="Reading position"
                   AutomationProperties.AutomationId="ReadingPositionLiveRegion" />

        <!-- TOC/Bookmarks/Highlights drawers (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-books-reader-hud-
             redesign-design.md) - ReaderListDrawer owns the scrim/Popup/header/airspace-safe
             positioning now; each screen just supplies its own list as DrawerContent, unchanged from
             what used to sit directly under each Popup. -->
        <!-- Grouped/collapsible TOC (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-books-reader-hud-redesign-
             design.md) - TocGroups (built by BookReaderScreenViewModel.RebuildTocGroups from each
             chapter's EPUB-nav-derived PartTitle) renders a group header only when PartTitle is
             non-null; an ungrouped chapter is still its own single-item group with no visible header,
             so this is one template, not two parallel grouped/ungrouped paths. FB2/MOBI/PDF chapters
             have no PartTitle (that format-specific limitation is disclosed in IBookTextSource.cs) and
             so render exactly as a flat list, same as before this feature. -->
        <views:ReaderListDrawer PanelBackground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static reader:ReaderPanelBackgroundConverter.Instance}}" PanelForeground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static views:ReaderChromeForegroundConverter.Instance}}" IsOpen="{Binding IsTocOpen}" HeaderText="Chapters" OverlayReference="{Binding #RootGrid}" ScrimPressed="OnScrimPointerPressed">
            <views:ReaderListDrawer.DrawerContent>
                <DockPanel>
                <!-- Go to page (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-books-reader-paged-scroll-modes-design.md §6.5): book pages, or print pages when the file has them.
                     Shown once the page map is ready. Enter jumps; the drawer closes. -->
                <StackPanel DockPanel.Dock="Top" Spacing="4" Margin="16,0,16,12"
                            IsVisible="{Binding GoToPageTotalText, Converter={x:Static conv:StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}">
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto">
                        <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="fieldLabel" Text="Go to page" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,8,0" />
                        <TextBox Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding GoToPageText}" KeyDown="OnGoToPageKeyDown"
                                 AutomationProperties.Name="Go to page" AutomationProperties.AutomationId="BookReaderGoToPage" />
                        <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Classes="pbTextMeta" Text="{Binding GoToPageTotalText}" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="8,0,0,0" />
                    </Grid>
                    <TextBlock Classes="pbTextMeta" Text="{Binding GoToPageError}" Foreground="{DynamicResource PbDangerBrush}"
                               IsVisible="{Binding GoToPageError, Converter={x:Static conv:StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}" />
                </StackPanel>
                <ScrollViewer>
                    <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding TocGroups}" Margin="8,0,8,16"
                                  AutomationProperties.AutomationId="BookReaderTocList">
                        <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="models:BookTocGroup">
                                <StackPanel Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                    <Button Classes="tocGroupHeader" Command="{Binding ToggleExpandedCommand}"
                                            IsVisible="{Binding PartTitle, Converter={x:Static conv:StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}"
                                            AutomationProperties.Name="{Binding PartTitle}">
                                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*">
                                            <fi:SymbolIcon Grid.Column="0" Symbol="ChevronDown" FontSize="{StaticResource PbIconSizeXs}" Margin="0,0,6,0"
                                                           IsVisible="{Binding IsExpanded}" />
                                            <fi:SymbolIcon Grid.Column="0" Symbol="ChevronRight" FontSize="{StaticResource PbIconSizeXs}" Margin="0,0,6,0"
                                                           IsVisible="{Binding !IsExpanded}" />
                                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding PartTitle}" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                                        </Grid>
                                    </Button>
                                    <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Chapters}" IsVisible="{Binding IsExpanded}" Margin="12,2,0,4">
                                        <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="models:BookChapterSummary">
                                                <Button Classes="tocRow" Classes.active="{Binding IsActive}" Content="{Binding Title}"
                                                        Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:BookReaderScreenViewModel)DataContext).GoToChapterCommand}"
                                                        CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                                            </DataTemplate>
                                        </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                    </ItemsControl>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </DataTemplate>
                        </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    </ItemsControl>
                </ScrollViewer>
                </DockPanel>
            </views:ReaderListDrawer.DrawerContent>
        </views:ReaderListDrawer>

        <!-- Notes (books redesign §5.3): highlights and bookmarks in one panel with Book Detail's kind chips; the reader's only Export. -->
        <views:ReaderListDrawer PanelBackground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static reader:ReaderPanelBackgroundConverter.Instance}}" PanelForeground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static views:ReaderChromeForegroundConverter.Instance}}" IsOpen="{Binding IsNotesOpen}" HeaderText="Notes" DrawerWidth="340" OverlayReference="{Binding #RootGrid}" ScrimPressed="OnScrimPointerPressed">
            <views:ReaderListDrawer.DrawerContent>
                <DockPanel>
                    <StackPanel DockPanel.Dock="Top" Spacing="12" Margin="16,0,16,12">
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                            <Button Classes="filterChip" Classes.on="{Binding IsNotesAll}" Content="All"
                                    Command="{Binding SetNotesFilterCommand}" CommandParameter="{x:Static models:BookNoteKindFilter.All}" />
                            <Button Classes="filterChip" Classes.on="{Binding IsNotesHighlights}" Content="Highlights"
                                    Command="{Binding SetNotesFilterCommand}" CommandParameter="{x:Static models:BookNoteKindFilter.Highlights}" />
                            <Button Classes="filterChip" Classes.on="{Binding IsNotesBookmarks}" Content="Bookmarks"
                                    Command="{Binding SetNotesFilterCommand}" CommandParameter="{x:Static models:BookNoteKindFilter.Bookmarks}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8">
                            <Button Grid.Column="0" Classes="secondary sm" Classes.active="{Binding IsCurrentPositionBookmarked}"
                                    Command="{Binding ToggleBookmarkCommand}" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                    AutomationProperties.Name="Bookmark this page" AutomationProperties.AutomationId="NotesToggleBookmarkButton">
                                <Panel>
                                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8" IsVisible="{Binding !IsCurrentPositionBookmarked}"><fi:SymbolIcon Symbol="Bookmark" FontSize="{StaticResource PbIconSizeXs}" VerticalAlignment="Center" /><TextBlock Text="Bookmark this page" /></StackPanel>
                                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8" IsVisible="{Binding IsCurrentPositionBookmarked}"><fi:SymbolIcon Symbol="Checkmark" FontSize="{StaticResource PbIconSizeXs}" VerticalAlignment="Center" /><TextBlock Text="Bookmarked" /></StackPanel>
                                </Panel>
                            </Button>
                            <Button Grid.Column="1" Classes="ghost sm" Content="Export…" Command="{Binding ExportAnnotationsCommand}"
                                    AutomationProperties.AutomationId="ExportAnnotationsButton" />
                        </Grid>
                        <TextBlock Text="Drag across text in the page to highlight it." Classes="pbTextCaption" TextWrapping="Wrap" IsVisible="{Binding ShowNoteHighlights}" />
                    </StackPanel>
                    <ScrollViewer>
                        <StackPanel Margin="8,0,8,16" Spacing="8">
                            <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding ShowNoteHighlights}">
                            <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Highlights}" Margin="8,0,8,16"
                                      AutomationProperties.AutomationId="BookReaderHighlightsList">
                            <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                <DataTemplate x:DataType="models:BookHighlightSummary">
                                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" Margin="0,2">
                                        <Border Grid.Column="0" Width="8" CornerRadius="{DynamicResource PbRadiusSm}" Margin="6,4,10,4"
                                                Background="{Binding Color, Converter={x:Static views:HighlightColorConverter.Instance}}" />
                                        <Button Grid.Column="1" Classes="tocRow" HorizontalContentAlignment="Left" Padding="0,10"
                                                Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:BookReaderScreenViewModel)DataContext).GoToHighlightCommand}"
                                                CommandParameter="{Binding}">
                                            <StackPanel>
                                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding ChapterTitle}" FontSize="11" FontWeight="Bold"
                                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource PbTextMutedBrush}" />
                                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding Excerpt}" FontSize="13" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource PbTextMutedBrush}" Margin="0,2,0,0" />
                                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding Note}" FontSize="12" FontStyle="Italic" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxLines="2" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource PbTextMutedBrush}" Margin="0,2,0,0"
                                                           IsVisible="{Binding Note, Converter={x:Static conv:StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}" />
                                            </StackPanel>
                                        </Button>
                                        <Button Grid.Column="2" Classes="deleteRow" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:BookReaderScreenViewModel)DataContext).DeleteHighlightCommand}"
                                                CommandParameter="{Binding}" ToolTip.Tip="Remove highlight"
                                                AutomationProperties.Name="Remove highlight">
                                            <fi:SymbolIcon Symbol="Dismiss" FontSize="{StaticResource PbIconSizeXs}" />
                                        </Button>
                                    </Grid>
                                </DataTemplate>
                            </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                        </ItemsControl>
                            </StackPanel>
                            <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding ShowNoteBookmarks}">
                            <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Bookmarks}" Margin="8,0,8,16"
                                      AutomationProperties.AutomationId="BookReaderBookmarksList">
                            <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                <DataTemplate x:DataType="models:BookBookmarkSummary">
                                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" Margin="0,2">
                                        <Button Grid.Column="0" Classes="tocRow" HorizontalContentAlignment="Left"
                                                Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:BookReaderScreenViewModel)DataContext).GoToBookmarkCommand}"
                                                CommandParameter="{Binding}">
                                            <StackPanel>
                                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding ChapterTitle}" FontSize="11" FontWeight="Bold"
                                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource PbTextMutedBrush}" />
                                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding Excerpt}" FontSize="13" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource PbTextMutedBrush}" Margin="0,2,0,0" />
                                            </StackPanel>
                                        </Button>
                                        <Button Grid.Column="1" Classes="deleteRow" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:BookReaderScreenViewModel)DataContext).DeleteBookmarkCommand}"
                                                CommandParameter="{Binding}" ToolTip.Tip="Remove bookmark"
                                                AutomationProperties.Name="Remove bookmark">
                                            <fi:SymbolIcon Symbol="Dismiss" FontSize="{StaticResource PbIconSizeXs}" />
                                        </Button>
                                    </Grid>
                                </DataTemplate>
                            </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                        </ItemsControl>
                            </StackPanel>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </ScrollViewer>
                </DockPanel>
            </views:ReaderListDrawer.DrawerContent>
        </views:ReaderListDrawer>

        <!-- Highlight color/note popup - anchored to the just-completed selection or tapped highlight.
             ShouldUseOverlayLayer="False" was meant to force a real separate OS popup window rather
             than Avalonia's in-process overlay layer, to stay above the native WebView (see the
             airspace note above the NativeWebView element) - but per that same note, Program.cs's
             Win32PlatformOptions.OverlayPopups = true overrides this app-wide, so this popup is
             actually in-process/overlay-layer-rendered like every other overlay in this file, and
             likely has the SAME "covered by the WebView" bug the drawers had (2026-09-16) - NOT
             verified or fixed. Unlike the drawers, hiding the whole WebView while this is open isn't
             a clean fix here (it's a small, position-anchored popup meant to sit next to the still-
             visible selection/highlight it's about), so this needs its own design decision, not a
             copy of the drawer fix. -->
        <!-- Fixed 2026-10-27: the card is now shown in an owned OverlayHostWindow by code-behind (SetHighlightPopupOpen), the same fix the drawers got, because a Popup is embedded
             in the window and so painted underneath the NativeWebView (no highlight colours or Look up ever appeared). This holder only keeps the card while the window is closed. -->
        <Panel x:Name="HighlightPopupHolder" IsVisible="False">
            <Border x:Name="HighlightPopupCard" Background="{DynamicResource PbChromeBrush}" BorderBrush="{DynamicResource PbBorderBrush}"
                    BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="{DynamicResource PbRadiusLg}" Padding="16" Margin="0,8,0,0"
                    Focusable="True" KeyDown="OnHighlightPopupKeyDown">
                <StackPanel Spacing="10" Width="260">
                    <!-- Dictionary card (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-books-slice4b-dictionary-design.md section 4): replaces the colours while a word is looked up. -->
                    <StackPanel Spacing="8" IsVisible="{Binding IsLookingUp}">
                        <TextBlock Text="{Binding LookUpWord}" FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="15" />
                        <TextBlock Text="{Binding LookUpStatus}" IsVisible="{Binding HasLookUpStatus}" TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12"
                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource PbTextMutedBrush}" />
                        <ProgressBar Minimum="0" Maximum="1" Value="{Binding DictionaryProgress}" IsVisible="{Binding IsDownloadingDictionary}" />
                        <ScrollViewer MaxHeight="220" VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
                            <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding LookUpGroups}">
                                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                    <DataTemplate x:DataType="dict:DictionaryPosGroup">
                                        <StackPanel Spacing="2" Margin="0,0,0,8">
                                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding Pos}" FontStyle="Italic" FontSize="12" Foreground="{DynamicResource PbTextMutedBrush}" />
                                            <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Senses}">
                                                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                                    <DataTemplate x:DataType="dict:DictionarySense">
                                                        <StackPanel Margin="0,0,0,4">
                                                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding Definition}" TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="13" />
                                                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding Example}" TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12" FontStyle="Italic"
                                                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource PbTextMutedBrush}"
                                                                       IsVisible="{Binding Example, Converter={x:Static conv:StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}" />
                                                        </StackPanel>
                                                    </DataTemplate>
                                                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                            </ItemsControl>
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </DataTemplate>
                                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                            </ItemsControl>
                        </ScrollViewer>
                        <Button Classes="secondary" Content="Download dictionary" Command="{Binding DownloadDictionaryCommand}"
                                IsVisible="{Binding OfferDictionaryDownload}" />
                        <Button Classes="secondary" Content="Look up online" Command="{Binding LookUpOnlineNowCommand}"
                                IsVisible="{Binding OfferOnlineLookUp}" />
                        <Button Classes="ghost" Content="Back" Command="{Binding BackFromLookUpCommand}" HorizontalAlignment="Left" />
                    </StackPanel>
                    <Button Classes="secondary" Content="Look up" Command="{Binding LookUpCommand}"
                            HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                            AutomationProperties.AutomationId="BookReaderLookUp">
                        <Button.IsVisible>
                            <MultiBinding Converter="{x:Static BoolConverters.And}">
                                <Binding Path="CanLookUp" />
                                <Binding Path="IsNotLookingUp" />
                            </MultiBinding>
                        </Button.IsVisible>
                    </Button>
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8" HorizontalAlignment="Center" IsVisible="{Binding IsNotLookingUp}">
                        <Button Classes="chromeIcon" Width="32" Height="32" Padding="0"
                                Command="{Binding PickHighlightColorCommand}" CommandParameter="{x:Static entities:BookHighlightColor.Yellow}"
                                AutomationProperties.Name="Yellow highlight">
                            <Border Classes="themeSwatch" Width="24" Height="24" Background="{DynamicResource PbHighlightYellowBrush}" />
                        </Button>
                        <Button Classes="chromeIcon" Width="32" Height="32" Padding="0"
                                Command="{Binding PickHighlightColorCommand}" CommandParameter="{x:Static entities:BookHighlightColor.Green}"
                                AutomationProperties.Name="Green highlight">
                            <Border Classes="themeSwatch" Width="24" Height="24" Background="{DynamicResource PbHighlightGreenBrush}" />
                        </Button>
                        <Button Classes="chromeIcon" Width="32" Height="32" Padding="0"
                                Command="{Binding PickHighlightColorCommand}" CommandParameter="{x:Static entities:BookHighlightColor.Blue}"
                                AutomationProperties.Name="Blue highlight">
                            <Border Classes="themeSwatch" Width="24" Height="24" Background="{DynamicResource PbHighlightBlueBrush}" />
                        </Button>
                        <Button Classes="chromeIcon" Width="32" Height="32" Padding="0"
                                Command="{Binding PickHighlightColorCommand}" CommandParameter="{x:Static entities:BookHighlightColor.Pink}"
                                AutomationProperties.Name="Pink highlight">
                            <Border Classes="themeSwatch" Width="24" Height="24" Background="{DynamicResource PbHighlightPinkBrush}" />
                        </Button>
                    </StackPanel>
                    <TextBox Text="{Binding HighlightPopupNote}" PlaceholderText="Add a note (optional)" AcceptsReturn="False" IsVisible="{Binding IsNotLookingUp}" />
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" IsVisible="{Binding IsNotLookingUp}">
                        <Button Grid.Column="0" Classes="ghost sm" Content="Remove highlight" Command="{Binding DeleteHighlightFromPopupCommand}"
                                IsVisible="{Binding IsEditingExistingHighlight}" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Foreground="{DynamicResource PbDangerBrush}" />
                        <Button Grid.Column="1" Classes="ghost sm" Content="Cancel" Command="{Binding CancelHighlightPopupCommand}" />
                    </Grid>
                </StackPanel>
            </Border>
        </Panel>

        <!-- Search drawer - a left drawer now (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-books-reader-hud-
             redesign-design.md), not a centered top dropdown: it's a list of results, same family as
             TOC/Bookmarks/Highlights above, and the design's overlay-direction decision is "lists
             open left." HasSearchBox="True" pins the search TextBox above the results instead of a
             plain static header. -->
        <views:ReaderListDrawer PanelBackground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static reader:ReaderPanelBackgroundConverter.Instance}}" PanelForeground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static views:ReaderChromeForegroundConverter.Instance}}" IsOpen="{Binding IsSearchOpen}" DrawerWidth="320" OverlayReference="{Binding #RootGrid}" ScrimPressed="OnScrimPointerPressed"
                                 HasSearchBox="True" SearchBoxWatermark="Search this book"
                                 SearchBoxText="{Binding SearchQuery, Mode=TwoWay}">
            <views:ReaderListDrawer.DrawerContent>
                <DockPanel>
                    <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Top" Text="No matches" FontSize="13" Margin="8,0,0,6"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource PbTextMutedBrush}"
                               IsVisible="{Binding HasNoSearchResults}" />
                    <ScrollViewer>
                        <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding SearchResults}" Margin="8,0,8,16">
                            <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                <DataTemplate x:DataType="models:BookSearchResult">
                                    <Button Classes="resultRow" HorizontalContentAlignment="Left"
                                            Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:BookReaderScreenViewModel)DataContext).GoToSearchResultCommand}"
                                            CommandParameter="{Binding}">
                                        <StackPanel>
                                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding ChapterTitle}" FontSize="11" FontWeight="Bold"
                                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource PbTextMutedBrush}" />
                                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding Excerpt}" FontSize="13" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource PbTextMutedBrush}" Margin="0,2,0,0" />
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </Button>
                                </DataTemplate>
                            </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                        </ItemsControl>
                    </ScrollViewer>
                </DockPanel>
            </views:ReaderListDrawer.DrawerContent>
        </views:ReaderListDrawer>

        <!-- Font & Theme sheet (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-books-reader-hud-redesign-design.md)
             - shared ReaderSettingsSheet control, grouped into mini-cards instead of 8 flat sections.
             HasTypographyControls="True": EPUB gets the full Typography/Spacing/Theme card set. -->
        <views:ReaderSettingsSheet IsOpen="{Binding IsFontSheetOpen}" HasTypographyControls="True"
                                    Settings="{Binding Settings}"
                                    SheetBackground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static views:ReaderChromeBackgroundConverter.Instance}}"
                                    SheetForeground="{Binding Settings.Theme, Converter={x:Static views:ReaderChromeForegroundConverter.Instance}}"
                                    SetFontFamilyCommand="{Binding SetFontFamilyCommand}"
                                    SetLineSpacingCommand="{Binding SetLineSpacingCommand}"
                                    SetThemeCommand="{Binding SetThemeCommand}"
                                    HasAutoHideToggle="True" AutoHideToggle="{Binding AutoHideChromeToggle}"
                                    HasReadingAids="True" LayoutPaged="{Binding IsPaged}" SetLayoutCommand="{Binding SetLayoutCommand}" RulerOn="{Binding IsRulerOn}" AutoScrollOn="{Binding IsAutoScrolling}" LookUpOnline="{Binding LookUpOnline}"
                                    HasSpeech="{Binding HasSpeech}" SpeakOn="{Binding IsSpeaking}" SpeechVoice="{Binding SpeechVoice}" SpeechVoices="{Binding SpeechVoices}"
                                    ThemeOptions="{x:Static views:ReaderSettingsSheet.AllThemes}"
                                    OverlayReference="{Binding #RootGrid}"
                                    ScrimPressed="OnScrimPointerPressed" />

    </Grid>
</UserControl>
